          "message": "chore: Remove obsolete root Dockerfile and examples-container workflow (#2284)\n\nRemoves unused top-level `Dockerfile` from repository root and the\nassociated CI workflow that depended on it.\n\n**Context:**\n- The Dockerfile builds a multi-stage Rust examples container but is not\nreferenced by any CI workflows, documentation, or build scripts\n- The `.github/workflows/examples-container.yml` workflow was the only\nworkflow using this Dockerfile\n\n**Files Removed:**\n- `/Dockerfile` (root of repository)\n- `/.github/workflows/examples-container.yml` (CI workflow)\n\nBoth files are obsolete and no longer needed for the repository's build\nand deployment processes.\n\n\n\n*This pull request was created as a result of the following prompt from\nCopilot chat.*\n> Remove the top-level Dockerfile (path: Dockerfile) from the\nrepository. Action items:\n> \n> - Delete the file at Dockerfile (root of repo).\n> - Ensure the change is a single commit with a clear commit message:\n\"Remove obsolete Dockerfile\".\n> - Open a pull request with the title \"Remove root Dockerfile\" and a\ndescription that explains why the file is being removed (e.g., obsolete,\nnot used by CI, duplicate, or replaced by other tooling). The PR\ndescription should list the path removed and any quick notes for\nmaintainers about potential follow-ups (search for any references to\nDockerfile in CI or docs and mention if none found or if further updates\nmay be required).\n> \n> Do not modify any other files. Leave base branch unspecified (use\nrepository default).\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> Remove the top-level Dockerfile (path: Dockerfile) from the\nrepository. Action items:\n> \n> - Delete the file at Dockerfile (root of repo).\n> - Ensure the change is a single commit with a clear commit message:\n\"Remove obsolete Dockerfile\".\n> - Open a pull request with the title \"Remove root Dockerfile\" and a\ndescription that explains why the file is being removed (e.g., obsolete,\nnot used by CI, duplicate, or replaced by other tooling). The PR\ndescription should list the path removed and any quick notes for\nmaintainers about potential follow-ups (search for any references to\nDockerfile in CI or docs and mention if none found or if further updates\nmay be required).\n> \n> Do not modify any other files. Leave base branch unspecified (use\nrepository default).\n\n\n</details>\n\n*This pull request was created as a result of the following prompt from\nCopilot chat.*\n> Remove the top-level Dockerfile (path: Dockerfile) from the\nrepository. Action items:\n> \n> - Delete the file at Dockerfile (root of repo).\n> - Ensure the change is a single commit with a clear commit message:\n\"Remove obsolete Dockerfile\".\n> - Open a pull request with the title \"Remove root Dockerfile\" and a\ndescription that explains why the file is being removed (e.g., obsolete,\nnot used by CI, duplicate, or replaced by other tooling). The PR\ndescription should list the path removed and any quick notes for\nmaintainers about potential follow-ups (search for any references to\nDockerfile in CI or docs and mention if none found or if further updates\nmay be required).\n> \n> Do not modify any other files. Leave base branch unspecified (use\nrepository default).\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in\nour [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: MingweiSamuel <6778341+MingweiSamuel@users.noreply.github.com>",
