          "id": "4f76b1f1fee7faa60c873f72afc4e43ef3b8d3b6",
          "message": "test(hydro_lang): update tests to avoid synchronous cycles, #2080 (#2731)\n\n### Documentation (`location/mod.rs`)\n\n- Rewrote `forward_ref` doc comment: clarifies it's for forward\nreferences, points to `Tick::cycle()` for feedback, and documents the\npanic on synchronous cycles.\n- Replaced the doctest with a valid DAG-style forward reference (no\ncycle).\n\n### Test fixes (`stream/mod.rs`, `keyed_stream/mod.rs`)\n\n- Fixed 7 sim tests that created synchronous cycles by routing\ncycled-back data through a second process via `.send(&node2,\nTCP.fail_stop().bincode()).send(&node, TCP.fail_stop().bincode())`.\n\n### Simulator docs (`sim/runtime.rs`)\n\n- Added comments on `TopLevelStreamOrderHook` and\n`TopLevelKeyedStreamOrderHook` explaining why `assume_ordering` outside\na tick gets special treatment: it's the only place where causality\n(cycled-back data interleaving with pending input) can be observed, so\nthe simulator releases elements one at a time to explore all\ninterleavings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>",
