          "id": "fc8add41380f856316b7b356ecc2c398740b5f58",
          "message": "feat(hydro_lang): support singleton refs on all operators via `ClosureExpr`, fix #2713 (#2872)\n\nReplaces the ad-hoc `singleton_refs: Vec<(syn::Ident, HydroNode)>` field\nthat was only on `HydroNode::Map` with a new `ClosureExpr` type that\nbundles\na closure expression with its captured singleton references.\n\nKey changes:\n\n- New `ClosureExpr` struct in `compile/ir/mod.rs` with:\n  - `expr: DebugExpr` — the closure's token stream\n  - `singleton_refs: Vec<(syn::Ident, HydroNode)>` — captured singletons\n- Helper methods: `new()`, `deep_clone()`, `transform_children()`,\n`emit_tokens()`\n- Implements Clone, Hash, Serialize, Debug, Display, ToTokens,\nFrom<syn::Expr>, From<DebugExpr>\n\n- All closure-bearing HydroNode variants now use `ClosureExpr`:\n  Map, FlatMap, FlatMapStreamBlocking, Filter, FilterMap, Inspect,\n  Partition, Fold, Scan, ScanAsyncBlocking, FoldKeyed, Reduce,\n  ReduceKeyed, ReduceKeyedWatermark\n\n- `HydroRoot::ForEach` also uses `ClosureExpr`\n\n- `with_singleton_capture()` now returns `ClosureExpr` directly instead\nof\n  a tuple, simplifying all call sites\n\n- Added `with_singleton_capture` to Stream::filter, flat_map_ordered,\nflat_map_unordered, inspect, and partition (previously only map had it)\n\n- Code generation (`emit_tokens`) handles singleton ref rewriting for\nall\noperators: Map, FlatMap, FlatMapStreamBlocking, Filter, FilterMap,\nInspect\n\n- Updated `transform_children` and `deep_clone` to properly\ntraverse/clone\n  singleton refs on all closure-bearing nodes\n\n- Updated viz/render.rs to extract `.expr` when passing to display\nfunctions\n\n- Updated all IR snapshot tests (hydro_lang serde_test, hydro_test IR\nsnapshots)\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>",
