          "message": "feat(hydro_lang): add by_mut support to stream operator closures: flat_map_ordered, flat_map_unordered, filter, partition, filter_map, inspect, flat_map_stream_blocking, for_each (#2942)\n\nExtended the `by_mut` singleton capture mechanism to all tier 1 and tier\n2 Stream\noperators. When a `SingletonMut` (or other mutable handoff ref) is\ncaptured in a\nclosure, the operator now enforces commutativity and idempotence safety:\n\n- If the stream has non-deterministic ordering (NoOrder), the closure\nmust provide\n  a `commutative = ...` proof annotation, or the code won't compile.\n- If the stream has non-deterministic retries (AtLeastOnce), the closure\nmust provide\n  an `idempotent = ...` proof annotation.\n- If the stream has TotalOrder + ExactlyOnce, no annotations are needed.\n\nChanges:\n- hydro_lang/src/properties/mod.rs: Added\n`ValidMutBorrowCommutativityFor` and\n`ValidMutBorrowIdempotenceFor` traits for borrow-based operators\n(filter, partition,\n  inspect) where the closure takes `&T` input.\n- hydro_lang/src/live_collections/stream/mod.rs: Updated\nflat_map_ordered,\nflat_map_unordered, filter, partition, filter_map, inspect,\nflat_map_stream_blocking\nto accept `FnMut` with `StreamMapFuncAlgebra` props and validity trait\nbounds.\nUpdated for_each to accept `FnMut` (trivially safe since it requires\nTotalOrder +\n  ExactlyOnce).\n- hydro_lang/src/live_collections/singleton.rs: Updated flat_map_ordered\nand\n  flat_map_unordered to match the new Stream signatures.\n- hydro_lang/src/live_collections/optional.rs: Same as singleton.\n- Added compile-fail tests for filter, flat_map_ordered, and filter_map\nwith by_mut\n  on NoOrder streams.\n- Added positive compile-only tests for by_mut in filter,\nflat_map_ordered,\n  filter_map, and inspect on TotalOrder streams.\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>\nPR: #2936\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>",
