          "id": "dd97ba458ef032bd10d65c9dad2d2d7c0a74c1cb",
          "message": "refactor(hydro_lang): make `DfirBuilder` statement placement location-aware (#3029)\n\nBehavior-neutral refactor of the `DfirBuilder` abstraction in\npreparation for emitting Hydro tick regions as root-level DFIR `loop {\n... }` blocks (hydro-project/hydro#2902). All generated DFIR is\nbyte-identical to before.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Replace `get_dfir_mut` with `add_dfir_at`** on the `DfirBuilder`\ntrait. Instead of handing callers a raw `&mut FlatGraphBuilder`,\nstatements are now submitted together with their `LocationId`, letting\nthe builder decide *where* they go. This is the hook that will later\nallow production codegen to route tick-located statements into the\ntick's `loop { ... }` context (via the `current_loop` parameter of\n`FlatGraphBuilder::add_dfir`). ~38 call sites in `emit_core`\nmechanically rewritten.\n\n- **New `ProdDfirBuilder` struct** replacing the `impl DfirBuilder for\nSecondaryMap<LocationKey, FlatGraphBuilder>`. It wraps the\nper-root-location graph map (public `graphs` field, so `emit()`'s return\ntype is unchanged); tick→loop tracking state will be added here in the\nfollow-up.\n\n- **New lifetime-selection trait methods**\n`tick_state_lifetime(op_location)` and\n`cross_tick_state_lifetime(op_location)`, with default implementations\nreturning `'tick` / `'static` (used by both production and simulation).\nOnce tick regions live inside DFIR loops, the production builder will\noverride these to return `'none` / `'loop` for tick-located operators\n(pending the lifetime unification in hydro-project/hydro#3023, which\nwould make the current defaults valid inside loops verbatim). All\nhardcoded `quote!('tick)` / `quote!('static)` persistence choices in\n`emit_core` (join, cross_join, cross_singleton, difference/anti_join,\njoin_multiset_half, fold/scan/fold_keyed, reduce/reduce_keyed,\nreduce_keyed_watermark, enumerate, unique) now go through these methods;\nlifetime computation moved inside the `Builders` match arms since it is\nonly needed there.\n\n- **`SimBuilder`**: `get_dfir_mut` moved from the trait impl to an\ninherent method (still used internally by its hook machinery);\nimplements the new `add_dfir_at`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p hydro_lang --features build,sim,viz,deploy` — all pass,\nincluding `compile/ir` and `sim` snapshot tests.\n- `cargo test -p hydro_test --lib` — all 53 pass; golden DFIR/IR\nsnapshots unchanged (no `.snap.new` produced).\n- `cargo clippy -p hydro_lang --features build,sim,viz,deploy` clean;\n`cargo fmt` applied.\n\nCo-authored-by: Infinity 🤖 <infinity@hydro.run>",
